{
  "_comment": [
    "D2 - the language-detection test set. Forty short strings.",
    "",
    "Every string is the length a real query is: three to twelve syllables. That",
    "is the point. Statistical detectors are trained on paragraphs and are",
    "unreliable here, and the half of the Vietnamese cases written without",
    "diacritics is where they fail hardest.",
    "",
    "'expect' is the language a Vietnamese-speaking human would assign. Cases",
    "marked hard=true are the ones where langdetect is expected to be wrong;",
    "they are the reason this module exists rather than a one-line import.",
    "",
    "Owner: Deval Patel."
  ],
